 regular status updates to customers and internal stakeholders Who We're Looking For 4-7 years of experience in accounting, audit, advisory, or related customer-facing roles Strong accounting foundation, with the ability to speak credibly about close, reconciliations, revenue recognition (ASC 606), and core finance workflows Excellent communication skills and the presence to work directly with customers and senior stakeholders Systems-minded and excited to learn implementation work, even if you have not formally held an implementation title before Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple workstreams at once Comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment while maintaining high attention to detail Experience working cross-functionally with technical and non-technical teams Experience in Big 4, SaaS or at a technology company is a plus Life at Rillet Grow with us. Take meaningful ownership, expand your scope, and make an impact as Rillet scales. Competitive pay and meaningful equity. Be rewarded for the value you help create. Benefits that support you. We offer medical and dental coverage, including up to 100% of employee premiums and 90% of dependent premiums, along with a 401(k), flexible PTO, nine company-wide holidays, and paid parental leave for eligible employees. Better together. We’re hybrid-first, with teams centered in New York City and San Francisco, as well as select remote roles. Our offices are stocked with snacks, we regularly provide lunch and dinner, and we make time to connect as a team. Compensation: $100K – $150K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges Zone A • $100K – $150K • Offers Equity Zone B • $100K – $140K • Offers Equity Zone C • $100K – $130K • Offers Equity Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
