    schema:datePosted "2026-08-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "We are supporting an international Oracle HCM implementation and are looking for an experienced Senior Oracle HCM Time & Labour Consultant to support the client during a challenging phase of its global payroll transformation. The consultant will join an existing Oracle HCM project team and provide hands-on functional and technical expertise within the Oracle HCM Time and Labor (T&L) module. The main focus of the assignment is on time-related payroll elements and Oracle Fast Formula / conversion formulas. General Oracle Time & Labour implementation knowledge is expected, but the client is specifically looking for a senior specialist who can independently analyze, configure, and resolve complex time-to-payroll requirements. The role is particularly suitable for an experienced Oracle HCM consultant who combines strong Time & Labour configuration expertise with a good understanding of the interaction between time data, payroll elements, formulas, work schedules, and downstream payroll processes. Framework Conditions Start: ASAP Duration: 5 months Capacity: approx. 3 days per week Location: Remote Language: English Level: Senior Contract Type: Freelance Tasks Act as Senior Oracle HCM Time & Labour Consultant within an international Oracle HCM and payroll transformation project Configure, analyze, and optimize Oracle HCM Time and Labor Design, adapt, and troubleshoot Oracle Fast Formula / conversion formulas Configure and resolve issues related to time-related payroll elements Support work schedules, shifts, time entry rules, time calculation rules, and related time configurations Analyze complex time calculation, payroll integration, and configuration issues and perform root-cause analysis Support testing, defect resolution, stabilization, and payroll-related validation activities Work closely with HR, Payroll, HR IT, implementation partners, and other Oracle HCM consultants Requirements Several years of hands-on experience as an Oracle HCM Cloud Consultant Strong implementation experience with Oracle HCM Time and Labor / Time & Labour Proven hands-on expertise with Oracle Fast Formula and conversion formulas Strong understanding of time-related payroll elements and time-to-payroll processes Solid knowledge of work schedules, shifts, time rules, time calculations, and related Oracle HCM configurations Experience troubleshooting complex functional and technical Oracle HCM Time & Labour issues Experience working in international Oracle HCM implementation or transformation projects Fluent English and the ability to work independently in a senior consulting role Nice to Have Experience in global or multi-country payroll transformation projects Experience integrating Oracle HCM Time & Labour with external payroll providers Knowledge of payroll interfaces and time-to-payroll data flows Experience with Oracle Payroll Experience with multi-country Oracle HCM rollouts Experience supporting SIT, UAT, payroll testing, or parallel payroll runs Experience in complex international HR technology environments Previous experience joining an existing Oracle HCM implementation during a critical project phase Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
